    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-07T18:04:09+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T18:04:09+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:34:09Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:34:09Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred well south of SA will continue to drift eastwards over the weekend, while a developing low pressure system and trough in WA move close to the SA border. The high drifts southeast of Tasmania by Monday as the low moves across western SA on Monday and northern SA on Tuesday before clearing to the east later. Another high develops south of the bight on Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-07T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds south to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h increasing to 25 to 40 km/h in the late evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny day. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Leigh Creek at night. Winds east to southeasterly 35 to 50 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of raised dust west of Leigh Creek in the morning and afternoon. Medium chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day then tending east to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of a thunderstorm with little or no rainfall. Winds northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 25 with daytime temperatures reaching 34 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Oodnadatta in the morning and afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
